@startuml wiring
' LocalAiRobot — "Wiring at a glance" connection map (full design: 3 sensors + camera + face).
' This source lives next to its render. Regenerate in place (writes wiring.png here):
'   plantuml -tpng docs/images/wiring.puml
' No Graphviz needed: !pragma layout smetana uses PlantUML's pure-Java layout engine.
' Palette via stereotypes (draw.io pastels), hidden with `hide stereotype`:
'   io #DAE8FC/#6C8EBF = compute / power-in   model #FFF2CC/#D6B656 = PWM bridge
'   data #D5E8D4/#82B366 = sensor / camera     motor #F8CECC/#B85450 = motor / actuator
'   store #F5F5F5/#666666 = note / bus
!pragma layout smetana
hide stereotype
title LocalAiRobot — wiring at a glance (3-sensor array + camera + face; two isolated power domains, common ground)

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 12
  FontSize 12
  BorderThickness 1
  BackgroundColor<<io>> #DAE8FC
  BorderColor<<io>> #6C8EBF
  BackgroundColor<<model>> #FFF2CC
  BorderColor<<model>> #D6B656
  BackgroundColor<<data>> #D5E8D4
  BorderColor<<data>> #82B366
  BackgroundColor<<motor>> #F8CECC
  BorderColor<<motor>> #B85450
  BackgroundColor<<store>> #F5F5F5
  BorderColor<<store>> #666666
}

' ---- motor / LiPo domain ----
rectangle "2S 7.4V LiPo" as lipo <<motor>>
rectangle "ESC\n(+ 6V BEC)" as esc <<motor>>
rectangle "drive motor" as motor <<motor>>
rectangle "steering servo\n(DS3225)" as servo <<motor>>

' ---- PWM bridge ----
rectangle "PCA9685\n(I2C PWM bridge, 0x40)" as pca <<model>>

' ---- brain / UPS domain ----
rectangle "Raspberry Pi 5\n(+ Active Cooler)" as pi <<io>>
rectangle "UPS HAT (its own 18650)\nor 27W PSU on the bench" as ups <<io>>

' ---- sensors / camera / face (all Pi-side, brain domain) ----
rectangle "HC-SR04P  front" as sonF <<data>>
rectangle "HC-SR04P  left" as sonL <<data>>
rectangle "HC-SR04P  right" as sonR <<data>>
rectangle "Pi Camera V2 NoIR\n(IMX219)" as cam <<data>>
rectangle "Face screen\n(3.5 inch USB-C)" as face <<io>>

' ---- connections (labels = what's on the wire) ----
lipo --> esc : 7.4 V
esc --> motor : motor drive
esc --> pca : ch0: signal + V+ rail (6V BEC) + GND
pca --> servo : ch1: signal / V+ / GND
pca --> pi : VCC 3.3V + SDA(GPIO2) + SCL(GPIO3) + GND
sonF --> pi : 3.3V + GND + TRIG(GPIO23) + ECHO(GPIO24)
sonL --> pi : 3.3V + GND + TRIG(GPIO5) + ECHO(GPIO6)
sonR --> pi : 3.3V + GND + TRIG(GPIO20) + ECHO(GPIO21)
cam --> pi : CSI ribbon (Pi-5 22->15 adapter)
face --> pi : USB-C -> /dev/ttyACM0
ups --> pi : 5V (its own battery)

note bottom of pca
  **Two isolated power domains** (LiPo -> motor/servo, UPS/PSU -> Pi): never bridge the battery positives,
  but tie **ALL grounds** together (Pi <-> PCA9685 <-> ESC) or the PWM won't register.
  The PCA9685 **V+ rail = the ESC's 6V BEC**, not the Pi. All 3 HC-SR04**P** run at 3.3V, so every ECHO is Pi-safe (no divider).
  Camera (CSI), face (USB-C) and the 3 sensors are all Pi-side / brain-domain.
end note
@enduml
